# Banned copy phrases

**Full messaging rules:** `docs/messaging-guide.md` · **Stats:** `lib/site.ts` only.

Never use these in customer-facing strings (`app/`, `components/`, `lib/*-copy.ts`, `lib/site.ts`, funnel libs).

| Banned | Why | Write instead |
|--------|-----|---------------|
| **—** (em dash) | AI/marketer voice; hard to read on mobile | Use a period, comma, colon, or parentheses instead |
| **quiz** (for Score Path) | Parents don't take a quiz | **SAT Score Path** |
| prep (as noun or modifier) | means nothing specific | "program," "practice," "tutoring," or name what's actually happening |
| **gains** (funnel copy) | tutor-ad jargon | "improve," "points," "movement" |
| **points leaking**, **cost points**, **what costs points**, **costing points** | tutor-ad jargon | "what they keep missing," "skills holding their score back" |
| **point leak(s)**, **biggest leaks**, **points are hiding**, **see where points hide** | tutor-ad jargon | "skills they keep missing," "weakest skills," "what the diagnostic ranks" |
| **generic prep**, **prep plan**, **generic review**, **generic lessons**, **generic advice** (SAT copy) | vague + "prep" | name what failed: "group class," "Khan course," "personalized weekly plan" |
| **Our read** | AI voice | drop it or say what the diagnostic shows |
| **broad review** | vague | "everything on the SAT" vs "5–6 skills" |
| **not a Khan stat**, **our program outcome, not** | awkward meta | state Illuminairy stats plainly — no DIY/Khan disclaimers |
| **District-wide**, **~115** (OSP), **20 hours on Official SAT Practice linked to** | implies Khan alone works | use `illuminairyFirstMonthOutcomeLine()` from `lib/site.ts` |
| **DIY promise**, **not the same as 20 hours on Khan** | defensive, weird | first-month outcome or skill-focus contrast only |
| engine, pivot engine | metaphor, not a feature | say what the 1:1s or sessions actually do |
| blueprint | vague planning metaphor | "schedule" or "personalized weekly plan" |
| rhythm, cadence | marketer shorthand for "schedule" | "the same schedule every week" |
| leverage | corporate jargon | "use" |
| ecosystem | meaningless in this context | name the actual parts |
| holistic | says nothing | describe what's included |
| empower, empowerment | empty verb | say what the student can do after |
| unlock, unlock potential | cliché | say what happens specifically |
| journey | vague | "personalized weekly plan" or "the program" |
| transform, transformation | overpromise | say what changes and how |
| seamless | never true, never specific | describe the actual experience |
| robust | filler adjective | drop it or say what makes it strong |
| curated | overused | "chosen" or "picked" |
| elevate | vague verb | say what improves and by how much |
| cutting-edge | cliché | name the specific thing |
| world-class | unprovable | use a specific credential |
| best-in-class | unprovable | use a specific credential |
| synergy | corporate jargon | say what works together and why |
| deep dive | cliché | "focus on" or "work through" |
| game-changer | hyperbole | say what's different and why it matters |
| next-level | empty modifier | drop it |
| proven (without citing proof) | unsubstantiated | cite the study or drop it |
| structured (as adjective for program) | brand-voice ban | "personalized weekly plan" or describe what's in it |
| personalized (without saying how) | vague | say what the mentor does differently for each student |
| reinforce / reinforces | vague | "your student works the same problem types until they stop getting them wrong" |
| human explanation layer | marketer metaphor | "a mentor who explains why you got it wrong" |
| score jump, big jump | tutoring-ad jargon | "a score competitive for their list," "in line with their GPA" |
| boost (their/your) score, score boost, bump their score | app-ad tone | "a stronger August score," "improve on the August test" |
| close the gap, add 100 points, +150 points | implied guarantee | "map their target on the consultation" |
| sitting, sittings | stiff / clinical | "test," "attempt," "retake," "test day," "next test date" |
| supercharge scores, skyrocket scores | hype | name program mechanics or drop |
| get into [school], guaranteed admission | admission promise | "competitive for their list," "keeps options open" |
| in range for admission | misreads middle 50% | "within the middle 50% of submitters — not a guarantee" |
| fit call | off-brand CTA | **Strategy Call** |
| **locked in**, **lock in**, **what you locked in**, **what clicked** | tutor-ad / vague session recap | name the skill or step: "Skills from this session," "what we covered," "Skill Diagnostic is booked" |

## Funnel product names (required)

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| quiz, assessment quiz | **SAT Score Path** |
| diagnostic on the call | **Skill Diagnostic** (2 hr 14 min, after Strategy Call) |
| consultation / fit call | **Strategy Call** (15 min advisory) |

## No negative framing

Headlines, titles, and lead copy must state what we **do**, not what we don't do or what's wrong with others.

Contrast clauses: what **we do better** — not awkward meta ("not a Khan stat") or trashing competitors.

## General rule

If a phrase could describe any company's product, it's too vague. If Brianna already corrected it once, check `docs/messaging-guide.md` before rewriting.
